{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"ef48e947a4c70e998653430bb13a9d08a072ac9319e2842cade50995f0f1d32c","digest":{"component_or_area":"pytest repo-isolation infrastructure (tests/_isolation.py, tests/conftest.py)","key_entities":["tests/_isolation.py","tests/conftest.py","pytest_sessionfinish","_no_repo_commits","porcelain()","head()","git status --porcelain","git rev-parse HEAD","GIT_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS","subprocess.TimeoutExpired","_run_process"],"problem_keywords":["subprocess timeout","git probe","pytest hook","session fixture","liveness","unbounded blocking","test isolation"],"propositions":["Repository isolation Git probes (porcelain and head) execute without subprocess timeout, allowing hung Git children to keep pytest alive indefinitely after test completion","Monkeypatched subprocess.run in test fixtures can contaminate autouse teardown guards before pytest restores the original module, causing test-local timeout doubles to incorrectly fail the safety boundary","Read-only repo-isolation probes must execute with a fixed 5-second watchdog and re-raise subprocess.TimeoutExpired explicitly rather than collapsing it to None","Both head() and porcelain() must bind the real subprocess.run at module import to isolate the safety guard from test-time subprocess monkeypatches, and must preserve the real sleep primitive during probe execution"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787605778113427001,"uuid":"db85fc6c-324e-4338-88d4-d5629f9939d3"}